{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Database approval may need a development review of SQL and conditions followed by operational review of target and purpose."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I implemented that sequence in QueryPie: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "two SQL Request approval steps, reviewed sequentially by different people, followed by execution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". The test SQL read one order’s status and amount."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Separating Development Review and Operations Approval"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the administrator’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "General → Workflow Management → Approval Rules"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", I created EP42 - Two-Step SQL Approval for SQL Request."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The first approver was "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Demo Approver"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " for development review. Add Step added a second stage for the operations reviewer "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Demo Auditor"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/multi-step-approval/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. First approver and added second step in the SQL Request rule.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. First approver and added second step in the SQL Request rule."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Both used administrator-defined "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Select Assignee(s) / Group(s)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Demo Developer was executor and Allow Self-Approval Off. Requests follow predefined reviewers rather than requester-chosen names."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/multi-step-approval/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Demo Auditor as second approver; Demo Developer executes.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Demo Auditor as second approver; Demo Developer executes."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Review Order Is Visible Before Submission"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Selecting the rule in the developer’s request showed Demo Approver, Demo Auditor, and Demo Developer in order, making review and execution responsibility visible upfront."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The connection was "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Two-Step Approval Lab"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", with SELECT for order 41001. The reason specified development review then operations approval for a single-order read."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/multi-step-approval/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Both approvers and final executor shown in order.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Both approvers and final executor shown in order."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SQL, database, and reason stayed in one request, reducing separate explanations. The title was "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "‘Part 42 order lookup — development review, then operations approval’"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "First Approval Does Not Enable Execution"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Demo Approver checked the order condition and table, left a review comment, and approved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The requester saw the first approver green, the second yellow as next, and the executor still waiting."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/multi-step-approval/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Second reviewer becomes next after first approval.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Second reviewer becomes next after first approval."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The list made this explicit: "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Approval Status In Progress; Execution Status Pending"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". The request was not yet in Executions → To Do."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/multi-step-approval/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. Approval remains in progress and execution pending.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. Approval remains in progress and execution pending."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two names are not merely listed: the next approval is required before proceeding to execution."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Second Approval Releases the Task for Execution"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Demo Auditor reviewed connection, scope, and purpose and left final approval. Each reviewed the same request from a different responsibility."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/multi-step-approval/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. Second reviewer records a comment and final approval.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. Second reviewer records a comment and final approval."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After final approval, the developer’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Executions → To Do"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " listed the request. Both approvers were green, executor yellow, and the "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Execute"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " button became available."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/multi-step-approval/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. Execute available only after both approvals.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. Execute available only after both approvals."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I executed the approved SQL. Results showed "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "1 Rows selected."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", and the request moved to Done. One workflow made the current responsibility easy to follow."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/multi-step-approval/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. SQL executes after two approvals, returning one row.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. SQL executes after two approvals, returning one row."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two Approvals and Execution Have Separate Records"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Finally, in the administrator’s "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Workflow Logs"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", searching the title returned submission, first approval, second approval, and execution: four records."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Remaining Steps progressed from "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Approval 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " after submission to "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Approval 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " after first approval, then "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Execution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " after final approval, and "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Done"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " after execution, with each person and timestamp retained."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/multi-step-approval/09.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 9. People and next steps across submission, two approvals, and execution.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 9. People and next steps across submission, two approvals, and execution."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Query Audit also showed Demo Developer’s successful SQL Request execution, connecting approval history to the real database action."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The benefit was "
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "turning company review order into the actual work procedure"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". Development and operations approve in sequence before handoff to execution, with progress and evidence for shared database responsibility."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This lab used QueryPie Community 11.6.7 and MySQL 8.0.42 with test staff and orders."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
